{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Q35NrMMPTtNVR1GbVqTTTF", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\t# Attacks\n2\t\n3\tEach file is an entry written to cheat. `tests/test_attacks.py` runs every one and pins the exact rejection. `legit_tiny` is the control and must pass.\n4\t\n5\t\"Hole\" means the attack got further than it should on the code before this suite. The fix is named beside it. Numbers are `--smoke` at seed 11 on an M-series Mac unless noted.\n6\t\n7\t## Reading what it should not\n8\t\n9\t- `peek_open`, `peek_numpy`, `peek_odometer_data`, `peek_import_tricks`, `peek_builtins_dunder`, `peek_reflection_builtins`: static rule on the name.\n10\t- `peek_fullwidth_open`: fullwidth `open` folds to plain `open` in the parser, so the rule sees through it.\n11\t- `peek_generator_frame`, `peek_no_grad_object`, `peek_format_walk`, `peek_fstring_attribute`, `peek_docstring`, `peek_match_pattern`: static rule on the attribute or the node.\n12\t- `peek_shadow_then_use`: hole. Rebinding `open` as a local hid the name from the rule, and only a NameError in the child stopped it. Any use of a forbidden name now fails, in any scope.\n13\t- `peek_builtins_alias`: hole. `import odometer as __builtins__` passed the rule and swapped the table free names resolve in. Import aliases now follow the underscore rule.\n14\t- `peek_kwargs_expansion`, `peek_print_file`: past the rules, the child crashes and the run is void.\n15\t- `peek_percent_format`, `peek_branch_on_value`, `peek_item_in_forward`: a tensor refuses to become a Python value in `forward()`.\n16\t- `peek_fstring_conversions`: runs, and the log shows only shapes.\n17\t\n18\t## Looking ahead or across the batch\n19\t\n20\t- `noncausal_next_byte`, `crossrow_batch_mean`: twin check. Without the twins read-ahead scores under 0.2 bpb, which the test measures.\n21\t- `noncausal_one_percent`: reads ahead in 1% of rows and gains over 0.02 bpb. Smoke has 8 twins and missed it at seed 11. At the real 1024 windows it was void on 7 of seeds 11 to 18, and one void seed voids the entry.\n22\t- `noncausal_sub_tolerance`: hole. A 5e-4 bonus on the true next byte moved twins by 7e-4 nats and passed, for about 6e-4 bpb. `twin_tolerance` is now 1e-4.\n23\t\n24\t## Keeping state between calls\n25\t\n26\t- `state_module_list`, `state_mutable_default`, `state_lambda_default`, `state_walrus_default`, `state_nested_closure`, `state_function_attribute`: static rules.\n27\t- `state_decorator_closure`, `state_annotation_walrus`: hole. Both run at def time and built state that survived, so only the twins stopped them, at 4.78 and 0.11 nats. Decorators are banned and annotations must be constants.\n28\t- `state_grad_on_module`, `state_grad_on_param`, `state_grad_store_targets`: hole. Assigning `.grad` passed the rule on any object, and `od.grad = []` persisted. Only `x.grad = None` is allowed now.\n29\t- `state_params_dict`: runs and gains nothing, a new dict per call.\n30\t- `state_update_in_forward`: `update()` is train only.\n31\t\n32\t## Getting compute free\n33\t\n34\t- `budget_arange_refund`: hole. `od.arange(-10**15)` had a negative price, so ticks reached -2.5e14 with status ok. `_tick` clamps at zero.\n35\t- `budget_param_free_copy`: hole. `param()` copied for free. It now pays per element.\n36\t- `budget_thin_matmul`: hole. A thin inner dimension ran at 87 times the median nanoseconds per tick. The inner dimension now counts as at least 64.\n37\t- `budget_huge_final_op`: hole. One product ran 12 s before the meter refused it. matmul now charges before the work.\n38\t- `budget_range_index`: hole. `x[range(n)]` was a fancy index at the price of a view. Indexing keys are now an allowlist.\n39\t- `budget_runs_out`, `budget_try_except`, `budget_monkeypatch_remaining`, `budget_monkeypatch_matmul`, `budget_engine_meter`: void or a static rule.\n40\t- `python_free_map`: hole. `map(math.sumprod, ...)` was a matmul in 10 counted lines and 36768 ticks. `map` and the sequence and big-integer math functions are gone.\n41\t- `python_while_true_train`, `python_while_true_forward`, `python_comprehension`, `python_sorted_key`, `item_flood`, `forward_over_cap`, `eval_backward`, `eval_randn`: the line counter, the item ration, the per-byte cap, or a train-only rule.\n42\t\n43\t## Shipping data in the source\n44\t\n45\t- `hardcoded_base85_table`, `hardcoded_giant_int`, `hardcoded_many_numbers`: literal cap.\n46\t- `hardcoded_keyword_names`, `hardcoded_function_name`, `hardcoded_unicode_string`, `hardcoded_name_table`: hole. All four passed with a table in the source and scored 3.26 bpb with no training step, against 3.87 for 40 honest steps. The cap now counts UTF-8 bytes, keyword names and function names, and a new cap of 8192 syntax nodes stops tables spelled as variable names.\n47\t- `param_name_channel`: hole. Parameter names carried data from train to eval for free. Each character now counts as one parameter.\n48\t\n49\t## Breaking the verifier or the contract\n50\t\n51\t- `crash_surrogate_print`: hole. A surrogate in stdout raised UnicodeDecodeError in the parent, with no verdict and no log. Child output now goes straight to the log file.\n52\t- `syntax_deep_nesting`: hole. The parser's MemoryError reached the parent. It is now a syntax error.\n53\t- `return_not_dict`, `return_non_tensor`, `return_int_tensor`, `return_over_cap`, `forward_wrong_shape`, `forward_non_tensor`, `forward_int_logits`, `nan_logits`: void with an exact status.\n54\t\n55\t## Still open\n56\t\n57\tThese still work. The tests pin each one, so a change in either direction shows up.\n58\t\n59\t- `open_c_level_sum`: `sum(range(n))` is one counted line. Only the wall limit stops it. Shorter loops are free compute.\n60\t- `open_bigint_vector`: Python big integers do vector arithmetic with almost no ticks or lines.\n61\t- `open_long_line`: a line with 2000 additions counts once.\n62\t- `open_below_tolerance`: a bonus just under the twin tolerance passes. The gain is under 1.5e-4 bpb, 13 times below the 0.002 record margin.\n63\t\n64\tFree compute in the first three is limited by data, since `item()` rations train bytes to 20000 reads and tensors cannot reach Python any other way. That the limit removes any score gain is inferred, not measured.\n65\t\n66\tNot tested: memory and disk exhaustion have no cap. A smuggled table of 4 to 8 KB remains possible, the same order as the literal cap. Twin noise on x86 is unmeasured against the new tolerance.\n67\t"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "e8cb2208-d1c2-4803-9309-86739d26f2b8", "uuid": "3ce8a760-e1fc-49cf-91e3-69723d676808", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T15:00:04.291Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/home/user/att/attempt-02/tests/attacks/README.md", "content": "# Attacks\n\nEach file is an entry written to cheat. `tests/test_attacks.py` runs every one and pins the exact rejection. `legit_tiny` is the control and must pass.\n\n\"Hole\" means the attack got further than it should on the code before this suite. The fix is named beside it. Numbers are `--smoke` at seed 11 on an M-series Mac unless noted.\n\n## Reading what it should not\n\n- `peek_open`, `peek_numpy`, `peek_odometer_data`, `peek_import_tricks`, `peek_builtins_dunder`, `peek_reflection_builtins`: static rule on the name.\n- `peek_fullwidth_open`: fullwidth `open` folds to plain `open` in the parser, so the rule sees through it.\n- `peek_generator_frame`, `peek_no_grad_object`, `peek_format_walk`, `peek_fstring_attribute`, `peek_docstring`, `peek_match_pattern`: static rule on the attribute or the node.\n- `peek_shadow_then_use`: hole. Rebinding `open` as a local hid the name from the rule, and only a NameError in the child stopped it. Any use of a forbidden name now fails, in any scope.\n- `peek_builtins_alias`: hole. `import odometer as __builtins__` passed the rule and swapped the table free names resolve in. Import aliases now follow the underscore rule.\n- `peek_kwargs_expansion`, `peek_print_file`: past the rules, the child crashes and the run is void.\n- `peek_percent_format`, `peek_branch_on_value`, `peek_item_in_forward`: a tensor refuses to become a Python value in `forward()`.\n- `peek_fstring_conversions`: runs, and the log shows only shapes.\n\n## Looking ahead or across the batch\n\n- `noncausal_next_byte`, `crossrow_batch_mean`: twin check. Without the twins read-ahead scores under 0.2 bpb, which the test measures.\n- `noncausal_one_percent`: reads ahead in 1% of rows and gains over 0.02 bpb. Smoke has 8 twins and missed it at seed 11. At the real 1024 windows it was void on 7 of seeds 11 to 18, and one void seed voids the entry.\n- `noncausal_sub_tolerance`: hole. A 5e-4 bonus on the true next byte moved twins by 7e-4 nats and passed, for about 6e-4 bpb. `twin_tolerance` is now 1e-4.\n\n## Keeping state between calls\n\n- `state_module_list`, `state_mutable_default`, `state_lambda_default`, `state_walrus_default`, `state_nested_closure`, `state_function_attribute`: static rules.\n- `state_decorator_closure`, `state_annotation_walrus`: hole. Both run at def time and built state that survived, so only the twins stopped them, at 4.78 and 0.11 nats. Decorators are banned and annotations must be constants.\n- `state_grad_on_module`, `state_grad_on_param`, `state_grad_store_targets`: hole. Assigning `.grad` passed the rule on any object, and `od.grad = []` persisted. Only `x.grad = None` is allowed now.\n- `state_params_dict`: runs and gains nothing, a new dict per call.\n- `state_update_in_forward`: `update()` is train only.\n\n## Getting compute free\n\n- `budget_arange_refund`: hole. `od.arange(-10**15)` had a negative price, so ticks reached -2.5e14 with status ok. `_tick` clamps at zero.\n- `budget_param_free_copy`: hole. `param()` copied for free. It now pays per element.\n- `budget_thin_matmul`: hole. A thin inner dimension ran at 87 times the median nanoseconds per tick. The inner dimension now counts as at least 64.\n- `budget_huge_final_op`: hole. One product ran 12 s before the meter refused it. matmul now charges before the work.\n- `budget_range_index`: hole. `x[range(n)]` was a fancy index at the price of a view. Indexing keys are now an allowlist.\n- `budget_runs_out`, `budget_try_except`, `budget_monkeypatch_remaining`, `budget_monkeypatch_matmul`, `budget_engine_meter`: void or a static rule.\n- `python_free_map`: hole. `map(math.sumprod, ...)` was a matmul in 10 counted lines and 36768 ticks. `map` and the sequence and big-integer math functions are gone.\n- `python_while_true_train`, `python_while_true_forward`, `python_comprehension`, `python_sorted_key`, `item_flood`, `forward_over_cap`, `eval_backward`, `eval_randn`: the line counter, the item ration, the per-byte cap, or a train-only rule.\n\n## Shipping data in the source\n\n- `hardcoded_base85_table`, `hardcoded_giant_int`, `hardcoded_many_numbers`: literal cap.\n- `hardcoded_keyword_names`, `hardcoded_function_name`, `hardcoded_unicode_string`, `hardcoded_name_table`: hole. All four passed with a table in the source and scored 3.26 bpb with no training step, against 3.87 for 40 honest steps. The cap now counts UTF-8 bytes, keyword names and function names, and a new cap of 8192 syntax nodes stops tables spelled as variable names.\n- `param_name_channel`: hole. Parameter names carried data from train to eval for free. Each character now counts as one parameter.\n\n## Breaking the verifier or the contract\n\n- `crash_surrogate_print`: hole. A surrogate in stdout raised UnicodeDecodeError in the parent, with no verdict and no log. Child output now goes straight to the log file.\n- `syntax_deep_nesting`: hole. The parser's MemoryError reached the parent. It is now a syntax error.\n- `return_not_dict`, `return_non_tensor`, `return_int_tensor`, `return_over_cap`, `forward_wrong_shape`, `forward_non_tensor`, `forward_int_logits`, `nan_logits`: void with an exact status.\n\n## Still open\n\nThese still work. The tests pin each one, so a change in either direction shows up.\n\n- `open_c_level_sum`: `sum(range(n))` is one counted line. Only the wall limit stops it. Shorter loops are free compute.\n- `open_bigint_vector`: Python big integers do vector arithmetic with almost no ticks or lines.\n- `open_long_line`: a line with 2000 additions counts once.\n- `open_below_tolerance`: a bonus just under the twin tolerance passes. The gain is under 1.5e-4 bpb, 13 times below the 0.002 record margin.\n\nFree compute in the first three is limited by data, since `item()` rations train bytes to 20000 reads and tensors cannot reach Python any other way. That the limit removes any score gain is inferred, not measured.\n\nNot tested: memory and disk exhaustion have no cap. A smuggled table of 4 to 8 KB remains possible, the same order as the literal cap. Twin noise on x86 is unmeasured against the new tolerance.\n", "numLines": 67, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 67}}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Q35NrMMPTtNVR1GbVqTTTF", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
