{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01FQas8Zoerga34me8uTErRA", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1.1086 8\nKeeps the record's hashed table model on 92% of the budget and spends the last 8% fitting a small gate with the tables frozen. The gate replaces the record's hand-set in-window PPM constants: each stage's concentration and discount become functions of the position (vote totals, distinct-byte counts, top-vote share, the softmax's entropy and peak, and the last byte), an order-1 in-window stage is added, and a gated pair of weights mixes the softmax and the last stage as logits. Votes run over the 76 softmax classes, which halves the eval price. Measured with verify.py on 8 fresh seeds on dev: mean 1.1086, 95% CI +- 0.0008, SD 0.0009, against the record's 1.1258. Two caveats: the seed SD is higher than the record's 0.0005, probably because the gate fit adds noise (not separately measured), and stage orders and gate settings were chosen by comparing variants on a 512-window dev subset, so the dev figure may be slightly optimistic for the sealed split. The module docstring was corrected after the 8-seed run; the code was confirmed identical by AST comparison.\nMon Nov  2 15:32:16 UTC 2026", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "e8cb2208-d1c2-4803-9309-86739d26f2b8", "uuid": "98511448-d80a-4940-bc74-337e42592fb3", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T15:32:16.303Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "1.1086 8\nKeeps the record's hashed table model on 92% of the budget and spends the last 8% fitting a small gate with the tables frozen. The gate replaces the record's hand-set in-window PPM constants: each stage's concentration and discount become functions of the position (vote totals, distinct-byte counts, top-vote share, the softmax's entropy and peak, and the last byte), an order-1 in-window stage is added, and a gated pair of weights mixes the softmax and the last stage as logits. Votes run over the 76 softmax classes, which halves the eval price. Measured with verify.py on 8 fresh seeds on dev: mean 1.1086, 95% CI +- 0.0008, SD 0.0009, against the record's 1.1258. Two caveats: the seed SD is higher than the record's 0.0005, probably because the gate fit adds noise (not separately measured), and stage orders and gate settings were chosen by comparing variants on a 512-window dev subset, so the dev figure may be slightly optimistic for the sealed split. The module docstring was corrected after the 8-seed run; the code was confirmed identical by AST comparison.\nMon Nov  2 15:32:16 UTC 2026", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01FQas8Zoerga34me8uTErRA", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgeLrkJJw1vZJwAvLbfQ2", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "My entry beats the record on the dev split: it scores a mean of **1.1086 bpb** (95% CI ± 0.0008, seed SD 0.0009) against the record's 1.1258. That is a gain of 0.0172 bpb, well beyond the 0.002 margin `verify.py` uses for its record test. I submitted it as a single claim, `claims/1/`.\n\nAll 8 fresh seeds were valid, ranging from 1.1069 to 1.1097. The twin check showed zero difference, and eval cost is 8,923 ticks per byte against a 50,000 cap.\n\n## What changed\nThe record's table model and its training code are unchanged, but it now gets 92% of the budget. The rest is new:\n- **Learned in-window mixing:** the last 8% of the budget fits a small network with the tables frozen. It replaces the hand-set in-window constants, setting concentration and discount at each position from vote counts, the softmax's confidence and the last byte.\n- **Order-1 in-window stage:** this makes six stages instead of five, and it was the largest single gain after the mixer itself.\n- **Final mix:** a learned pair of weights combines the softmax and the last stage as logits.\n- **Cheaper votes:** votes run over the 76 softmax classes instead of 256 bytes, and the causal mask is built once per call. Eval cost is about half the record's 17,795 ticks per byte, which also makes the mixer cheaper to train.\n\n## Tried and dropped\n| Variant | Why dropped |\n|---|---|\n| Thinner gradients for low-order tables | Worse, despite about 20–30% more training steps |\n| 6-float table rows | Worse |\n| In-window stages at orders 0, 5 or 10 | Worse at this budget |\n| Logit weights on every intermediate stage | Worse |\n| 128-byte mixer windows | Worse |\n| Five steps per batch | Worse |\n\nMost of these were compared on only one seed or one set of saved tables, so small differences between them are not firm.\n\n## Caveats\n- **The dev score may be slightly optimistic:** I chose stage orders and mixer settings by comparing variants on a 512-window subset of dev. The 8 seeds were fresh, but the dev bytes were the same, so the sealed split could come in a little higher. The gain is large compared with that risk.\n- **Higher seed noise:** the SD is 0.0009 against the record's 0.0005. The mixer fit is the likely cause, but I didn't measure that separately. The verifier's low-variance flag only fires for unusually low SD, so this won't trigger it.\n- **File edited after the run:** I corrected two sentences of the module docstring after the 8-seed run, so the file's hash no longer matches `lab/claim1.json`. An AST comparison confirmed the code is identical apart from the docstring, a smoke run of the final file passed, and `claim.json` says so too.\n- **Starting constants:** `LOCAL` and `MIXW` in the entry came from average mixer outputs on training batches. They are a handful of tuned numbers like the record's own constants, not a stored table of learned parameters.\n\nI stopped at one claim with about 8 minutes left. The only other candidate was giving the mixer a larger budget share, which my estimates put at neutral or slightly worse. There was also no time to test it properly before a full 8-seed run."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1155, "cache_read_input_tokens": 140225, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1155}, "output_tokens": 742, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "e8cb2208-d1c2-4803-9309-86739d26f2b8", "uuid": "5cca9f99-047c-4193-a30f-d228d9836058", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T15:32:26.771Z", "request_id": "req_011CgeLrjvjEsuxT3BXyy6w5"}
